# Test file to demonstrate error messages.
#
# This program is meant NOT to compile: every statement below is a mistake, and
# the point is to read what is reported. Every one of them is now caught before
# the program runs, so only the first is shown at a time — comment out a line
# to see the next.

# This will cause an undefined variable error with suggestion
Declare myVariable to be 10.
Print the value of myVarible.  # Typo: myVarible instead of myVariable

# This will cause an undefined function error
Call myFunctoin.  # Typo: myFunctoin

# This will cause a constant reassignment error
Declare PI to be always 3.14.
Set PI to be 3.  # Error: cannot reassign constant

# This will cause an argument count mismatch
Declare function add that takes a as number and b as number, and gives back a number, and does the following:
    Return a + b.
thats it.

Set result to be the result of calling add with 5.  # Missing second argument

# This will cause a division by zero error
Declare x to be 10.
Declare y to be 0.
Set result to be x / y.
